{:edb/db-before-t 9190 :edb/db-after-t 9191 :edb/tx-data [[13194139542503 50 #inst "2026-10-28T05:51:54.691Z" 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186144119 1075 #edb/ref 17592186725879 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186144119 1078 #edb/ref 17592186725879 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186147726 1071 "Find the general **nonzero real** solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\nx^2\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}=y^4-xy.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval with $x\\ne0$ where the solution is finite. Interpret cube roots as real cube roots." 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186147726 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n$x^{2}\\frac{dy}{dx} = y^{4} - xy$." 13194139542503 17592186576411 false] [17592186147726 1074 "For $x\\ne0$, write the equation in Bernoulli form:\n\n$$\ny'+\\frac1x y=\\frac1{x^2}y^4.\n$$\nWe seek the nonzero real solutions, so divide by $y^4$ and set $z=y^{-3}$. The chain rule gives $z'=-3y^{-4}y'$, hence\n\n$$\nz'-\\frac3x z=-\\frac3{x^2}.\n$$\nOn any interval avoiding $x=0$, an integrating factor is $I(x)=x^{-3}$, because $I'/I=-3/x$. Multiplying and integrating gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x^{-3}z)'&=-3x^{-5},\\\\\nx^{-3}z&=\\frac3{4x^4}+K,\\\\\nz&=\\frac3{4x}+Kx^3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nNow substitute $z=y^{-3}$ and absorb the factor $4$ into the arbitrary constant, writing $C=4K$:\n\n$$\ny^3=\\frac{4x}{3+Cx^4},\\qquad\n\\boxed{y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{4x}{3+Cx^4}}}.\n$$\nThe cube root is the **real** cube root, so its argument may be negative. Use intervals with $x\\ne0$ and $3+Cx^4\\ne0$; on these intervals the family is real, finite and nonzero. The invertible substitution $z=y^{-3}$ recovers every nonzero solution there.\n\nTo verify the result without imposing a positive branch, put $g(x)=4x/(3+Cx^4)$. Since $y^3=g(x)\\ne0$, implicit differentiation gives $y'=yg'/(3g)$, and\n\n$$\nx^2y'-y^4+xy\n=y\\left(\\frac{x^2g'}{3g}-g+x\\right)=0.\n$$\nThe original equation also admits the equilibrium solution $y=0$. It is excluded only by the question's explicit **nonzero** condition; it was lost when dividing by $y^4$ and must be checked separately." 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186216607 1078 #edb/ref 17592186216608 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186216612 1075 #edb/ref 17592186725878 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186216612 1078 #edb/ref 17592186725878 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186217793 1071 "Consider the inexact differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}x-({x}^{3}+2{y}^{4})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nIt is known that \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{4}{y}\n$$\n\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by \n\n$$\nP(x,y)={x}^{2}y,\\hspace{2em}Q(x,y)=-{x}^{3}-2{y}^{4}.\n$$\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(y)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.\n\n$\\hspace{2em}$ A suitable integrating factor is $I(y)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\hspace{2em}$ The general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant." 13194139542503 17592186576411 false] [17592186217793 1071 "Consider the inexact differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}y\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}x-({x}^{3}+2{y}^{4})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nIt is known that \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=\\frac{4}{y}\n$$\n\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by \n\n$$\nP(x,y)={x}^{2}y,\\hspace{2em}Q(x,y)=-{x}^{3}-2{y}^{4}.\n$$\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(y)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.\n\n$\\hspace{2em}$ A suitable integrating factor is $I(y)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\hspace{2em}$ The general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant.\n\nUse the displayed quotient only where it is defined, and use the integrating-factor method on regions with $y\\ne0$." 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186217793 1074 "For an integrating factor depending only on $y$, use\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\exp\\left(-\\int\\frac{P_y-Q_x}{P}\\,\\mathrm dy\\right).\n$$\nThe displayed quotient is evaluated where $P\\ne0$. Since it simplifies to $4/y$, we can choose\n\n$$\nI(y)=e^{-4\\ln|y|}=\\frac1{y^4},\\qquad y\\ne0.\n$$\nMultiplication gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{y^3}\\,\\mathrm dx+\n\\left(-\\frac{x^3}{y^4}-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm dy=0.\n$$\nThis equation is exact, because\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(\\frac{x^2}{y^3}\\right)\n=-\\frac{3x^2}{y^4}\n=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(-\\frac{x^3}{y^4}-2\\right).\n$$\nTo find a potential $F(x,y)$, integrate its $x$-derivative while holding $y$ fixed:\n\n$$\nF_x=\\frac{x^2}{y^3}\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\nF(x,y)=\\frac{x^3}{3y^3}+G(y).\n$$\nDifferentiate with respect to $y$ and match the other coefficient:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{x^3}{y^4}+G'(y)=-\\frac{x^3}{y^4}-2,\n\\qquad G'(y)=-2.\n$$\nTherefore the requested implicit general solution is\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\frac{x^3}{3y^3}-2y=c},\\qquad y\\ne0.\n$$\nIndeed, $\\mathrm dF=y^{-4}(P\\,\\mathrm dx+Q\\,\\mathrm dy)$, so the level curves give the original differential equation on the stated regions. Although the quotient formula initially requires $P\\ne0$, the resulting integrating factor and exact equation extend to $x=0$ whenever $y\\ne0$.\n\nThe original equation also admits $y=0$. That solution lies outside the question's explicit $y\\ne0$ region, where the integrating factor is undefined. The factor $1/3$ in the potential is necessary: omitting it changes $F_x$ and does not merely rename the arbitrary constant." 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186725878 1080 "\\frac{x^3}{3y^3}-2y=c" 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186725878 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186725878 1083 #uuid "4135e069-47f7-5fd9-aef2-f6794b685c8e" 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186725879 1080 "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{4x}{3+Cx^4}}" 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186725879 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139542503 17592186576411 true] [17592186725879 1083 #uuid "95b153b8-ee28-5e20-a56a-0e684c56347c" 13194139542503 17592186576411 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-4135e069-47f7-5fd9-aef2-f6794b685c8e" 17592186725878 "answer-95b153b8-ee28-5e20-a56a-0e684c56347c" 17592186725879} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
